# PLAN1 DOCS — initialize advertise vs ship 1 must

File: openOODA/audit/plan1_docs.oot
Wave 0 survey. Read only. Do not implement. Disk is the source.
Do not edit the public site. Do not edit ROADMAP.oot. Do not edit vscode.

## 1. Product path

VS Code starts native `ooda lsp` over stdio. Launch is
`vscode/extension.js` with `args: ["lsp"]` and
`vscode-languageclient`. That client sends standard Language
Server Protocol (LSP) messages. It does not send a `"prefix"`
key.

Product route on disk:
  `cli/main.oo` calls `run_ooda_lsp`.
  `cli/lsp_drive.oo` frames stdin and calls `lsp_build_reply`.
  `cli/lsp_reply.oo` builds the JSON-RPC result.

Help text still says initialize, hover, symbols, definition.
It does not name completion. Ship 1 must not edit `cli/main.oo`.

`ooda/lsp/` (`lsp/` in the ooda tree) is a catalog. It is not
the server. `cli/lsp/` is a twin of that catalog. Product CLI
does not import either folder. Do not grow those folders.

## 2. What initialize advertises NOW

File: `cli/lsp_reply.oo` method `initialize`. Exact result:

  {"capabilities":{"textDocumentSync":1,"hoverProvider":true,"documentSymbolProvider":true,"definitionProvider":true}}

Status: partial.

Present:
  textDocumentSync value 1 (full document)
  hoverProvider true
  documentSymbolProvider true
  definitionProvider true

Absent:
  completionProvider
  triggerCharacters
  textDocument/completion dispatch

Unknown methods return an empty string. A completion request
from VS Code gets no result.

Hover and definition already read `"line"` and `"character"`.
They call `lsp_src_offset` then `lsp_ident_at`. That is the
correct prefix path. Lock: `scripts/lsp_cursor_smoke.oo`.

## 3. What ooda/lsp advertises (not product)

File: `lsp/lsp_server.oo` function `lsp_server_capabilities_json`.
Exact capabilities object:

  {"capabilities":{"textDocumentSync":1,"completionProvider":{"resolveProvider":true,"triggerCharacters":[".","&",":"]},"hoverProvider":true}}

Status: residual as a product server. Smoke only as a catalog.

It does advertise completionProvider. Trigger list includes `&`.
It also sets resolveProvider true. It does not advertise
documentSymbolProvider or definitionProvider.

Completion dispatch is wrong for an editor:

  pfx = lsp_jsonrpc_extract_string(params, "prefix")

VS Code does not send `"prefix"`. The extract returns empty.
`scripts/lsp_server_smoke.oo` feeds a body with
`"prefix":"&Net"`. That test would still pass if the editor
path stayed broken. Do not copy this dispatch.

Catalog file `lsp/lsp_completion.oo` lists caps, keywords,
types, and builtins. Filter is `lsp_str_starts_with(label,
prefix)`. Empty prefix returns the full list. Label `&FsCap`
matches prefix `&`, `&F`, `&Fs`. It does not match prefix `Fs`.

DE2 must lift that catalog into new `cli/lsp_complete.oo`.
Same-folder imports only. Do not import `ooda/lsp/`.

## 4. What ship 1 must advertise

Done-when from `audit/plan_cli_lsp.oot` item 1:

  initialize JSON includes completionProvider.
  Trigger characters include `&`.

Keep the product capabilities that already work. Do not drop
hover, documentSymbol, or definition.

Required initialize result (minimum):

  {"capabilities":{"textDocumentSync":1,"hoverProvider":true,"documentSymbolProvider":true,"definitionProvider":true,"completionProvider":{"triggerCharacters":["&"]}}}

Rules:
  completionProvider must be present.
  triggerCharacters must include the character `&`.
  Extra triggers `.` and `:` are optional. Catalog uses them.
  Do not set resolveProvider true unless DE2 also handles
  method completionItem/resolve. Product unknown methods
  return empty. A true resolve flag can stall the editor.
  Boolean completionProvider true is weaker. Prefer the
  object form so `&` is a trigger.

DE1 owns `cli/lsp_reply.oo`. File is 220 lines. If dispatch
would pass 256 lines, split dispatch only. Do not rewrite
hover or definition.

## 5. Prefix law

Done-when item 3:

  Prefix uses line/character + lsp_ident_at.
  Not a fake `"prefix"` key.

Standard LSP CompletionParams (what VS Code sends):

  params.textDocument.uri
  params.position.line
  params.position.character
  optional params.context.triggerCharacter

There is no `"prefix"` field in the protocol.

Product helpers already exist in `cli/lsp_ident.oo`:
  lsp_json_int(body, "\"line\":")
  lsp_json_int(body, "\"character\":")
  lsp_src_offset(src, line, col)
  lsp_ident_at(src, offset)

Ship 1 must reuse that path. Load the file:// buffer the same
way hover does (`lsp_load_src`). Filter the catalog with the
ident at the cursor. Empty ident still returns the catalog.
Do not hang. Do not crash.

A test that only greps `completionProvider` in source is not
enough. HARN must drive rebuilt `bin/ooda lsp` with framed
JSON-RPC: initialize, then textDocument/completion on a file
URI. Assert `&FsCap` is in the result. Assert isIncomplete is
false.

## 6. Leading `&` on the ident

`lsp_ident_at` treats `_` and letters and digits as name
characters. It does not treat `&` as a name character.

Cursor on `Fs` in `&Fs` returns `Fs`.
Cursor just after typed `&` returns empty.

Catalog match needs a prefix that starts with `&` for
`&FsCap`. Plan says: include a leading `&`.

DE2 must look at the character before the ident. If that
character is `&`, put `&` in front of the ident. If the ident
is empty and the trigger or the previous character is `&`,
the prefix is `&`.

Do not change `lsp_ident_at` unless COORD assigns that file.
Default shared read-only: `cli/lsp_ident.oo`.

Target: buffer text `&Fs` at the cursor returns an item
labeled `&FsCap`.

## 7. Side-by-side

| item | product NOW | catalog ooda/lsp | ship 1 must |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| launch | bin/ooda lsp | not launched | keep product |
| hoverProvider | true | true | keep |
| documentSymbolProvider | true | absent | keep |
| definitionProvider | true | absent | keep |
| completionProvider | absent | present | required |
| trigger `&` | absent | present | required |
| resolveProvider | absent | true | omit or false |
| completion method | no dispatch | yes | required |
| prefix source | n/a | fake key | line/character + lsp_ident_at |
| `&Fs` → `&FsCap` | residual | smoke with fake key | required |
| empty prefix | n/a | full catalog | full catalog |
| cursor hover lock | done | n/a | must stay green |

Status words: done, smoke, partial, residual, open.

